---
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import DcfaPreparedDemo from '../../components/DcfaPreparedDemo.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import preparedDemo from '../../data/dcfa/prepared-demo-v1.json';

const colabUrl = 'https://colab.research.google.com/github/GepingChen/DCFA/blob/main/notebooks/DCFA_Custom_Analysis_Colab.ipynb';

for (const asset of Object.values(preparedDemo.assets)) {
  const path = resolve('public', asset.path.replace(/^\//, ''));
  const observed = `sha256:${createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(path)).digest('hex')}`;
  if (observed !== asset.sha256) {
    throw new Error(`TabCF-Agent prepared asset hash mismatch: ${asset.path}`);
  }
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TabCF-Agent — Auditable causal analysis agent"
  description="A static replay and user-owned Colab workflow for TabCF-Agent, an auditable agent for bounded continuous-treatment distributional-IV analysis."
>
  <header class="page-hero dcfa-hero">
    <div class="shell reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">TabCF-Agent · Auditable causal analysis</p>
      <h1>From a bounded question to evidence—or a visible stop.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">TabCF-Agent compiles a narrow natural-language request into a typed specification, delegates numerical work to deterministic tools, blocks unsupported claims, and keeps the displayed answer tied to verified evidence.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-title">
    <div class="shell reading-column">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">My contribution</p>
          <h2 id="scope-title">One causal design, one inspectable workflow.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>I designed and implemented the typed runtime, evidence ledger, support and failure gates, provider boundaries, independent artifact verifier, and the static/Colab release path shown here.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="scope-grid">
        <article><h3>Supported</h3><p>One continuous outcome Y, one continuous treatment X, one scalar instrument Z, no baseline covariates W, and treatment levels inside empirical support.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Blocked</h3><p>Binary or multi-arm treatment, added covariates, automatic instrument discovery, outside-support requests, provider failures, or evidence mismatches.</p></article>
      </div>

      <DcfaPreparedDemo demo={preparedDemo} colabUrl={colabUrl} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-contrast" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <div class="shell reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
      <h2 id="architecture-title">The language model never owns the number.</h2>
      <ol class="architecture-list">
        <li><strong>Prompt</strong><span>A bounded question names a supported mean or median summary or contrast.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Typed specification</strong><span>Gemini may compile symbolic low, center, and high labels; it receives no data rows or actual intervention values.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Deterministic tool</strong><span>The TabCF-Agent runtime validates roles, diagnostics, support, managed TabPFN output, and the requested estimand.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Evidence or stop</strong><span>A number appears only after evidence validation; unsupported or failed paths return no number.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="shell reading-column">
      <p class="eyebrow">Scope and limitations</p>
      <h2 id="limits-title">A released website tool, not a released scientific claim.</h2>
      <div class="limitations">
        <p>The replay is a synthetic, precomputed, development-only demonstration. It makes no API call when opened and does not prove instrument validity, identification, estimator accuracy, or agent superiority.</p>
        <p>The Colab route executes in the visitor's account. The question is sent to Google and confirmed Y/X/Z rows are sent separately to Prior Labs. Users must have permission to share their data and remain responsible for provider terms, quota, charges, and runtime availability.</p>
        <p>Managed-service traceability is not bitwise reproducibility. Locked Track T evidence still requires a fixed real TabPFN checkpoint and runtime image.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a href={preparedDemo.assets.verification_summary.path}>Inspect the public verification summary</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .dcfa-hero h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .hero-links {
    display: flex;
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.65rem 1.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .hero-links a {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 2.75rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .scope-grid article {
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .scope-grid article + article {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .scope-grid p,
  .limitations p,
  .architecture-list span {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .architecture-list {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .architecture-list li {
    display: grid;
    padding-block: 1rem;
    gap: 0.25rem 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .architecture-list strong {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .limitations {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 42rem) {
    .scope-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .scope-grid article:first-child {
      padding-right: 1.5rem;
    }

    .scope-grid article + article {
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }

    .architecture-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
